review_comments.body:
Even if constructing `rubyEnv` on-the-fly for a new version is currently nontrivial (which requires either expression files, dynamic derivation, or IFD), `finalAttrs` still facilitate overriding.

Inside the phases, you can reference an atteibute(say, `version`) with either `"$version"` or  `"${finalAttrs.version}"`.

```suggestion
stdenv.mkDerivation (finalAttrs:
  pname = "postal";
  version = "3.3.7";
  src = fetchFromGitHub {
    owner = "postalserver";
    repo = "postal";
    tag = finalAttrs.version;
    hash = "sha256-x00TGhJJRUoe/lPVPBDicZ+La1FU7OxkPUba/0/tx0I=";
  };

  rubyEnv = bundlerEnv rec {
    name = "postal-env-${finalAttrs.version}";
    ruby = ruby_3_4;
    gemdir = ./rubyEnv;
    gemset = import (gemdir + "/gemset.nix");
    groups = [
      "default"
      "oidc"
      "assets"
      "development"
      "test"
    ];
    gemConfig = defaultGemConfig;
  };
```

